 1. EWS endpoint URL for the target environment, the full path ending in /EWS/Exchange.asmx, and the Exchange version.
  2. Authentication methods accepted on the EWS virtual directory. Specifically, whether Basic authentication over TLS
     or OAuth is available for a service account, or NTLM only. The WWW-Authenticate header from an unauthenticated
     request is enough.
  3. Service account for the mailbox: account name in DOMAIN\user form and UPN. Please deliver the password through the
     agreed secure channel, not by email.
  4. The shared mailbox address for each environment (QA, UAT, production) and the rights granted to the service account
     on it: full-access delegate or application impersonation.
  5. Firewall confirmation for HTTPS from the MID server to the EWS host, and any proxy in the path.
  6. The internal CA certificate chain for the EWS host, so the MID server can verify TLS.
  7. EWS throttling policy applied to the service account.
  8. Mailbox folder to read from, folder to move processed mail into, and confirmation the account may set Outlook
     categories on messages.
  9. Password rotation policy for the service account and confirmation it is exempt from interactive MFA.
  10. Any planned date for migrating this mailbox to Exchange Online, since that changes the integration method.
